{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-47501",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{s}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{s(t+h)-s(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=7$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(7) & ≈\\frac{s(7+2)-s(7-2)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(9)-s(5)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{14-4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the velocity of Anna at the instant of time $t=7$ is $2.5\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
